WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:35.994 --> 00:37.495
This is your first time, huh?

00:37.579 --> 00:40.540
FIVE YEARS AGO

00:40.623 --> 00:42.625
You must be pretty desperate to do this.

00:43.543 --> 00:44.836
Sorry, I'm just curious.

00:46.504 --> 00:48.923
I mean, isn't marriage
supposed to be romantic?

00:49.966 --> 00:51.092
It is overrated.

00:52.469 --> 00:54.804
Still, there should be some attraction,
you know?

00:54.888 --> 00:57.807
First, you do a little mating dance,
then you get together.

00:58.308 --> 01:00.351
End of the day,
being married creates inertia.

01:00.435 --> 01:02.187
And that's just all a wedding does.

01:02.270 --> 01:03.521
Don't you think?

01:04.522 --> 01:07.734
I always fucking hated
that sense of inertia.

01:09.360 --> 01:12.614
Why is it such a big deal
to put two peoples' names on a document?

01:13.239 --> 01:16.618
All it is is a reminder that
neither person can trust their partner.

01:18.787 --> 01:21.372
Truth is, both of you know
it's not going to last.

01:22.373 --> 01:25.293
It's just a trap.
An easy way to tie each other down.

01:26.669 --> 01:27.712
And romance?

01:29.964 --> 01:31.800
A contract isn't romantic, is it?

01:33.676 --> 01:35.553
Do we need to certify romance at all?

01:37.430 --> 01:39.390
Who cares? It's all bullshit, right?

01:44.979 --> 01:47.065
So marriage is problematic for you?

01:47.148 --> 01:48.066
Well, no.

01:48.775 --> 01:50.068
Personally, I just…

01:52.737 --> 01:53.863
I loathe it.

01:57.283 --> 01:58.576
This wasn't a good idea.

02:00.078 --> 02:01.121
I'm gonna go.

02:02.413 --> 02:05.500
Listen, I'm dying.
I have six months left. Maybe four.

02:12.340 --> 02:14.843
Obviously, you would be
my first and last wife.

02:15.552 --> 02:17.345
If I said, "Let's get married…"

02:19.556 --> 02:20.682
you think you'd do it?

02:28.648 --> 02:34.571
THE TRUNK

02:36.656 --> 02:38.116
You know who I am, right?

02:39.284 --> 02:40.535
Yeah, I do.

02:41.828 --> 02:43.538
And how do you know who I am?

02:45.248 --> 02:46.541
Who cares, really?

02:55.842 --> 02:57.802
I knew someone
who took their own life in school,

02:57.886 --> 02:59.762
and I heard it might've been your fault.

03:00.763 --> 03:03.766
What I heard is they committed suicide
to get away from you.

03:04.350 --> 03:06.561
I must've been quite a bitch then, huh?

03:08.271 --> 03:11.357
That's how I know you,
not that I really think of you like that.

03:12.734 --> 03:13.902
Why do you say that?

03:15.403 --> 03:18.072
I guess it's hard to know
what would drive anyone to

03:19.073 --> 03:21.075
decide to take their own life like that.

03:23.328 --> 03:25.538
But in most cases, any excuse will do.

03:29.292 --> 03:30.335
Still, that doesn't mean

03:30.418 --> 03:33.004
you're not a conniving, dishonest,
and self-interested shrew.

03:35.590 --> 03:36.841
I do recall things

03:38.509 --> 03:40.011
in those days, In-ji.

03:42.388 --> 03:44.057
But the reason I remember you…

03:45.892 --> 03:47.936
Well, I'll tell you a bit later.
How's that?

04:09.624 --> 04:11.251
Don't get out. I have to get going.

04:11.960 --> 04:13.336
You stopped by our house?

04:14.587 --> 04:15.588
"Our house"?

04:17.423 --> 04:20.051
It's weird hearing you say "our house."

04:21.719 --> 04:23.054
You know, I met your wife too.

04:24.222 --> 04:25.098
Yeah?

04:25.807 --> 04:27.058
What did you think?

04:27.141 --> 04:28.142
She just…

04:29.227 --> 04:30.895
I mean, she really looks like a wife.

04:32.522 --> 04:34.357
You guys didn't know each other, did you?

04:35.775 --> 04:36.693
Oh…

04:38.069 --> 04:40.863
You'll never believe this,
but she actually went to our school.

04:43.616 --> 04:45.994
Hang in there,
even if the going gets tough with her.

04:46.869 --> 04:48.913
I still just wish I could trust you.

05:12.353 --> 05:13.980
She came because of the lights.

05:14.522 --> 05:18.651
Well, I gave her… a cup of tea.
We talked a little, and she left.

05:19.861 --> 05:21.029
I wasn't asking.

05:21.112 --> 05:23.281
If it were me, I bet I'd wanna ask.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.618
I can go with you
to the hospital.

05:27.702 --> 05:30.330
That hospital visit's next week.
I have to run errands.

06:03.196 --> 06:05.323
Are you still doing it?

06:06.366 --> 06:08.117
You're an expert. Help me out here.

06:27.428 --> 06:28.596
Well, does he hit you?

06:29.347 --> 06:30.807
Can you please just talk?

06:30.890 --> 06:32.850
Another bitch from South Korea.

06:32.934 --> 06:34.936
Hey, come on. Just ask me how I'm doing.

06:36.521 --> 06:38.356
I wanna know about you, honestly.

06:39.690 --> 06:42.026
Pleasure to see you, Yoo In-yeong.
How are you?

06:47.907 --> 06:48.950
I'm pregnant, actually.

06:50.493 --> 06:53.996
Maybe it's 'cause mine is dead,
but I really do wanna have a family.

06:55.415 --> 06:56.499
You have family, Ms. Noh?

06:56.582 --> 06:58.960
Your husband… Does he know?

07:00.461 --> 07:01.838
Well, I hope not.

07:02.672 --> 07:05.258
A family makes your life a lot harder,
just so you know.

07:06.384 --> 07:07.593
So why are you doing this?

07:08.094 --> 07:09.011
Why look for him?

07:09.095 --> 07:11.806
Wasn't it enough to find out
that he's still alive and well?

07:11.889 --> 07:13.933
Don't get me wrong. I like the money.

07:14.434 --> 07:16.561
Do you wanna marry him again or something?

07:18.312 --> 07:20.648
Or kill him and move on? That makes sense.

07:23.818 --> 07:24.944
Where is he right now?

07:29.740 --> 07:31.868
Prague, up until he moved to Hungary.

07:31.951 --> 07:33.911
My contact said that was two weeks ago.

07:34.412 --> 07:35.621
He's in Budapest.

07:39.041 --> 07:40.835
Stay in touch. Send updates, okay?

07:44.505 --> 07:47.133
I have dreams
where I find my siblings' bodies.

07:48.801 --> 07:52.430
Some nights, I can…
I can kind of make out their faces,

07:53.598 --> 07:57.477
but other times… they're so bloody,
I can't tell them apart.

07:58.311 --> 07:59.896
The dreams make me feel better.

08:01.147 --> 08:03.691
'Cause it's the not knowing
that drives people crazy.

08:06.819 --> 08:08.488
So what do you dream about, Ms. Noh?

08:12.617 --> 08:13.993
I don't dream anymore.

09:22.853 --> 09:25.439
Well, it looks like you forgot…

09:28.192 --> 09:29.735
…what day it is today.

10:21.037 --> 10:22.830
Son of a bitch.

10:43.267 --> 10:44.518
HAN JEONG-WON

10:47.146 --> 10:49.398
Mm-hmm. Yeah, turns out I have it.

10:49.482 --> 10:51.192
I found it while I was cleaning up.

10:51.275 --> 10:53.069
Yes, I know. You cherish it.

10:58.199 --> 10:59.575
Let's meet. I'll hand it over.

12:32.793 --> 12:34.044
There's no pain,

12:35.421 --> 12:37.423
in case that's why you are so upset.

12:54.190 --> 12:55.524
Going down.

13:10.623 --> 13:11.874
Sorry. Excuse me.

13:16.796 --> 13:18.297
Going down.

13:21.175 --> 13:23.636
Try to just clear your mind.
Focus on the numbers.

13:27.681 --> 13:28.808
They're just numbers.

14:04.635 --> 14:06.846
Would you like to schedule
Mrs. Noh an appointment

14:06.929 --> 14:08.055
with a plastic surgeon?

14:08.556 --> 14:09.557
- Oh, sure.
- Great.

14:09.640 --> 14:11.767
Can you tell me
when she might be available?

14:11.851 --> 14:13.394
Sorry. Just one minute.

14:15.604 --> 14:17.106
WIFE

14:18.440 --> 14:20.943
Sorry, I'm busy right now.
I'll call you later, okay?

14:21.443 --> 14:23.612
Will you be needing
any insurance paperwork?

14:23.696 --> 14:26.949
- No, that's all right.
- Okay. I can take your payment right here.

14:28.951 --> 14:29.952
Appreciate it.

14:41.630 --> 14:44.049
I'll get your meds, okay?
I'll be back soon.

14:57.438 --> 14:59.023
I've seen plenty of injuries and stuff,

14:59.106 --> 15:02.151
but I don't think
I've ever seen healing up close.

15:05.321 --> 15:06.614
Why do I feel…

15:08.616 --> 15:11.493
I won't be able to get this image
of that cut out of my head

15:11.577 --> 15:12.745
until you're healed?

15:18.751 --> 15:20.085
Obviously, you're stoic.

15:20.586 --> 15:22.087
Could you at least try to cry?

15:23.255 --> 15:25.633
I think I'd be more at ease
with everything.

15:38.604 --> 15:40.230
What are you doing Tuesday?

15:42.900 --> 15:46.028
Pretty sure I'm open.
We could have a quick wedding.

15:58.248 --> 16:00.501
NO RECENT MISSED CALLS

16:03.212 --> 16:06.048
Sorry, I'm busy right now.
I'll call you later, okay?

16:15.808 --> 16:18.310
Ugh, what is all this?
You guys were stuffing your faces.

16:18.394 --> 16:20.020
I ate too much.

16:20.604 --> 16:22.982
Guys, we talked about this.
You're not to eat snacks at night.

16:23.065 --> 16:24.650
All right. Brush your teeth.

16:25.150 --> 16:26.610
- No horsing around.
- Got ya!

16:26.694 --> 16:28.320
- Hey, stop messing around!
- Hey!

16:31.740 --> 16:34.410
Uh, my mom texted me yesterday.

16:34.952 --> 16:36.412
About those rice cakes…

16:37.997 --> 16:41.208
Why the… hell did I get married?

16:42.543 --> 16:44.003
Well, because I was…

16:45.504 --> 16:47.715
…basically the best in our W&L class?

16:47.798 --> 16:50.718
I was always the normal one,
but now I have the most screwed-up life.

16:50.801 --> 16:52.052
I don't get it.

16:52.553 --> 16:53.804
You need cash, Yoon-a?

16:54.513 --> 16:56.140
Keep it under two million won.

16:59.852 --> 17:01.437
Jeong-won's new wife. What's her name?

17:02.021 --> 17:04.064
- Why?
- I'd like to be her friend.

17:04.148 --> 17:05.983
- What?
- I've got nothing else.

17:06.066 --> 17:08.444
I don't have a career.
My husband's not exactly rich.

17:08.527 --> 17:10.029
There's no way I'm inheriting anything.

17:10.112 --> 17:12.448
I'm living with a business owner
who barely makes ends meet.

17:12.531 --> 17:14.033
All I have is my friends!

17:31.050 --> 17:34.094
It's standard procedure.
From the manual.

17:50.027 --> 17:51.195
The manual.

17:53.781 --> 17:56.450
Dude, uh, Yoon-a said…

17:56.533 --> 17:58.118
You need a new car, right?

17:58.202 --> 18:00.954
I'll get you one,
but I need your help tomorrow.

18:01.455 --> 18:04.083
What for? Oh my God. Are you in trouble?

18:04.917 --> 18:06.126
I need a witness

18:07.419 --> 18:09.296
'cause In-ji and I are getting married.

18:09.379 --> 18:12.883
I thought you guys weren't gonna have
a wedding. Wait, I'm the witness?

18:13.550 --> 18:16.261
Three o'clock.
They'll send a formal invite.

18:16.887 --> 18:17.846
Who? Uh…

18:31.401 --> 18:33.028
How's your wife's injury doing?

18:34.655 --> 18:37.449
Doing really well.
They removed her stitches.

18:38.075 --> 18:39.576
The doctor said it's healing fast.

18:39.660 --> 18:43.038
Although to be honest,
she might be stifling the pain.

18:44.414 --> 18:46.041
And you took her to the doctor?

18:47.209 --> 18:49.920
Well, yeah. You didn't know that?

18:54.842 --> 18:56.009
It was all my fault.

18:58.554 --> 18:59.847
It's nice that…

19:00.472 --> 19:02.599
…the two of you
are getting along so well.

19:10.524 --> 19:12.401
OH SE-EUN
OUR LOVER/THE ORPHAN/YOU

19:28.292 --> 19:31.211
Just a little keepsake
to commemorate our worst moment.

19:33.338 --> 19:34.715
How's it make you feel now?

19:46.685 --> 19:47.978
You're being cruel.

19:48.854 --> 19:49.813
How could you?

19:51.064 --> 19:53.275
I don't want you to take them. Got it?

19:56.069 --> 19:57.279
Just fight the urge.

20:02.951 --> 20:04.328
I'll do whatever you say.

20:07.247 --> 20:08.457
Our wedding is tomorrow.

20:21.345 --> 20:22.471
INBOX
NM: INVITATION

20:22.554 --> 20:24.139
GROOM HAN JEONG-WON
BRIDE NOH IN-JI

20:26.683 --> 20:29.895
AS THE WITNESS TO THIS WEDDING,
PLEASE NOTE THE FOLLOWING RULES

20:33.607 --> 20:36.902
It's a list of demands,
not… a wedding invite.

21:22.072 --> 21:24.074
How the hell do you put these things on?

21:39.798 --> 21:41.842
You know, I could've been undressed.

21:41.925 --> 21:45.387
If you weren't dressed by now,
it'd probably mean you're running away.

21:46.888 --> 21:48.432
I thought about it, actually.

21:48.515 --> 21:50.600
I never thought I'd be doing this again.

21:51.601 --> 21:54.646
Technically, we should've been married
after our first week together.

21:54.730 --> 21:56.648
We had to wait 'cause of the accident.

21:58.317 --> 22:00.277
Well, I mean, the manual says that.

22:00.360 --> 22:03.488
I thought I wouldn't have to deal with
formalities. Guess I was wrong.

22:19.129 --> 22:21.298
You're, uh, quite proficient.

22:21.381 --> 22:22.841
I have a way with things.

22:25.761 --> 22:29.890
My grandmother… said
I always had an eye for detail.

22:30.891 --> 22:35.187
She said those kinds of people
end up doing the work other people avoid.

22:35.687 --> 22:38.440
Guess I'm destined
for heartbreak and loneliness.

22:39.441 --> 22:40.567
You think?

22:43.445 --> 22:44.446
Uh, no.

22:50.160 --> 22:52.162
You know, I was gonna wear this suit
at the funeral.

22:52.245 --> 22:53.997
I knew that's what it was for.

22:54.498 --> 22:58.001
After all, this is your only black suit,
and you never wear suits anyway.

22:58.710 --> 23:02.130
I figured it was all part of the fact that
you're waiting for your father to die.

23:04.508 --> 23:07.677
Just think of this as
signing a one-year insurance contract.

23:08.637 --> 23:10.764
You just might have to pay a penalty
if you cancel.

23:13.433 --> 23:14.351
One year?

23:20.148 --> 23:21.358
Let's go.

23:38.333 --> 23:39.543
Can I see the plans?

23:41.086 --> 23:44.423
Perfect. Okay, so the space
you're looking at now is the library.

23:45.048 --> 23:46.258
And over here, this is…

23:46.341 --> 23:49.302
It's not too late.
Just say the word, and I'll call it off.

23:49.386 --> 23:51.972
So even at night,
it should have good natural light.

23:52.889 --> 23:55.725
Mm, the skylight is huge.
It's in a good spot.

23:56.309 --> 23:58.228
As for the lights, they'll go here.

23:58.854 --> 24:00.355
The purpose of this ceremony

24:00.439 --> 24:03.775
is to confirm and ratify the contract
between the two of you.

24:03.859 --> 24:06.903
The contract stipulates
total confidentiality

24:06.987 --> 24:10.073
between Mr. Han Jeong-won,
Ms. Noh In-ji, and NM.

24:10.782 --> 24:14.286
Legally, this marriage requires
no obligations.

24:14.369 --> 24:17.164
No duties. No records will be kept.

24:17.664 --> 24:19.458
In the case of a breach of contract,

24:19.541 --> 24:22.294
as stated
in your initial agreement with NM,

24:22.377 --> 24:25.172
either party
may potentially be subject to liability.

24:26.339 --> 24:28.300
Your contract will last one year.

24:28.383 --> 24:31.470
But if both parties agree,
you can extend the marriage.

24:32.512 --> 24:36.391
In the case of one party objecting,
the contract will be terminated for both.

24:36.475 --> 24:37.309
And you

24:38.643 --> 24:40.604
will never be allowed to… to speak again.

24:42.063 --> 24:43.773
As soon as you sign the contract,

24:43.857 --> 24:45.734
your marriage will begin.

25:08.965 --> 25:11.176
Mr. Han Jeong-won and Ms. Noh In-ji,

25:11.259 --> 25:14.095
you're now married legally
per your contract with NM.

25:14.679 --> 25:18.099
I'm honored to share this moment with you.
I wish you the best.

25:28.318 --> 25:34.991
MARRIAGE AGREEMENT
GROOM HAN JEONG-WON, BRIDE NOH IN-JI

25:35.075 --> 25:36.785
Standing over the ball,

25:36.868 --> 25:38.537
they've got a free kick
in a good position.

25:38.620 --> 25:40.247
They need to make this count.

25:40.330 --> 25:43.625
Oh, he's just gone
over the bar with that one though.

25:43.708 --> 25:46.002
I'll tell you what.
That was a really, really good shot.

25:46.086 --> 25:47.003
It was from distance.

25:47.087 --> 25:50.674
Not the easiest to get that…
get that up and in there, but…

25:50.757 --> 25:53.927
Ealing should've been able
to get it in there, but he was too slow.

25:54.010 --> 25:56.972
Looking back on it,
he should've done better with that.

25:57.055 --> 25:58.265
Oh, that's off.

25:58.348 --> 26:00.559
Tipped forward,
the center back headed it out,

26:00.642 --> 26:04.521
and now they're looking to go and build
some play from the right-hand side.

26:05.105 --> 26:06.481
They do have width.

26:06.565 --> 26:09.025
They have good width
on that right-hand side…

26:09.109 --> 26:10.402
What did you do before this?

26:11.152 --> 26:13.488
Uh, I'm not allowed to tell you that.

26:14.864 --> 26:15.907
Oh, you're not?

26:17.784 --> 26:19.452
Those lawyers must be incredible.

26:19.536 --> 26:22.789
I bet they could show up in a courtroom
and prove that Messi plays tennis.

26:25.709 --> 26:27.460
Why do other people do this anyway?

26:27.544 --> 26:31.715
Did you… ever think about asking why
your other husbands were doing this?

26:32.382 --> 26:35.135
He shoots!
And a great save there!

26:35.218 --> 26:36.761
I've been thinking about it.

26:37.762 --> 26:41.308
And I can see how, if you were lonely
or terminally ill and dying,

26:41.391 --> 26:43.184
you might wanna give this a whirl.

26:43.268 --> 26:46.146
It's still a fake marriage though.
Does it mean anything?

26:47.564 --> 26:49.941
People work so hard not to look lonely.

26:50.025 --> 26:52.694
They're even willing
to cling to a fake marriage.

26:54.487 --> 26:57.115
You can still be lonely,
even if you're with someone.

26:57.824 --> 26:59.659
They know that and get used to it.

27:00.368 --> 27:02.746
Separation anxiety. You become dependent.

27:03.830 --> 27:05.957
Isn't that the reason
you got married, at least?

27:09.169 --> 27:11.921
You became dependent.
Like separation anxiety.

27:12.589 --> 27:15.091
You knew perfectly well
that you'd still be lonely.

27:21.598 --> 27:22.641
Well, good night.

27:24.142 --> 27:25.143
By the way,

27:26.186 --> 27:28.313
we just kicked off our honeymoon, I guess.

27:31.149 --> 27:34.027
Peyton,
he did manage to get the equalizer.

27:34.110 --> 27:35.654
It's still one-one.

27:37.530 --> 27:40.200
I'm not so sure
they're really playing all out…

27:40.283 --> 27:43.119
IT'S NOT TOO LATE IF YOU STOP ME NOW
I WON'T GO THROUGH WITH IT

30:04.385 --> 30:05.720
Were you drowning?

30:08.014 --> 30:10.141
Is that what you were dreaming about?

30:12.685 --> 30:14.020
Just the usual.

30:16.189 --> 30:17.524
Try not to worry.

30:19.567 --> 30:21.694
The tidal waves can't reach you here.

31:27.677 --> 31:29.178
When I was sleeping, were you…

31:37.061 --> 31:37.979
Forget it.

31:38.563 --> 31:40.064
I think it was sleep paralysis.

31:41.399 --> 31:44.068
In case you wondered, it was all real.
I was by your bedside.

31:48.364 --> 31:51.576
Sleeping in the same room is protocol.
The manual says so.

31:53.745 --> 31:55.079
Were you drowning?

31:56.497 --> 31:58.374
Is that what you were dreaming about?

31:59.417 --> 32:00.835
Just the usual.

32:05.840 --> 32:07.091
Try not to worry.

32:08.885 --> 32:10.845
The tidal waves can't reach you here.

32:20.480 --> 32:21.814
Only in special situations

32:21.898 --> 32:24.233
is a married couple
not allowed to share a bed.

32:24.817 --> 32:26.319
"Special situations"?

32:26.402 --> 32:28.988
In the case of infectious diseases,
for example.

32:39.666 --> 32:41.250
What is Seo-yeon thinking?

32:42.418 --> 32:44.379
I need a companion, but not like this.

32:55.390 --> 32:57.433
My life's a train wreck as it is.

32:58.559 --> 33:01.229
So talk to my wife and find out
how much of this I need to take

33:01.312 --> 33:02.230
before she's satisfied.

33:03.147 --> 33:06.275
I wanted to let the year pass by quietly.
I told you.

33:06.359 --> 33:08.069
I don't get why that's so hard for you!

33:08.695 --> 33:10.989
- Why are you so upset right now?
- Upset?!

33:11.072 --> 33:13.032
I don't wanna care about this or you!

33:13.116 --> 33:15.618
I wanna go back to how things were!
I can't do this anymore!

33:17.286 --> 33:19.747
You mean
that you feel strongly about this?

33:20.331 --> 33:21.290
I do!

33:22.834 --> 33:23.793
I understand.

33:27.171 --> 33:28.381
I mean, we can

33:29.382 --> 33:31.634
probably address the sleeping arrangement.

34:14.677 --> 34:17.305
- Oh no, I'm stuck again.
- This was your idea.

34:17.388 --> 34:18.598
- Oh, I got ya.
- All right.

34:18.681 --> 34:21.017
- I got you. I got ya.
- Okay, you got me? There.

34:21.100 --> 34:23.603
- Turn, turn. Wait, try that again.
- Wait, wait. How?

34:23.686 --> 34:26.147
- Here. Do this with your leg.
- Oh, oh, like this?

34:29.275 --> 34:30.735
Pivot, pivot, pivot, pivot.

34:30.818 --> 34:32.737
Oh, uh, I just spun around.

34:32.820 --> 34:34.864
Oh, oh,
and then you go like this, okay?

34:34.947 --> 34:37.366
- That's it. Go down.
- I'm going down. I'm going.

34:37.450 --> 34:39.619
- Here I go.
- That's it.

34:39.702 --> 34:42.246
- Come on. Don't let go!
- I'm trying to hold on!

34:42.330 --> 34:43.706
- You're slipping!
- Help me.

34:47.251 --> 34:48.711
The new lights are coming.

34:48.795 --> 34:50.379
They'll be installed next week.

34:51.589 --> 34:53.841
Congrats on the wedding, honey.

35:15.780 --> 35:17.657
I'd like to inquire about
some drugs.

35:18.616 --> 35:20.827
The pills might not be
what the labels claim.

35:21.661 --> 35:23.121
I'd like to send them to you.

35:47.520 --> 35:49.313
Why the hell are you here so early?

35:49.856 --> 35:51.858
Hasn't it been a while since you cooked?

35:52.650 --> 35:54.902
What, is that bastard
coming back from the dead?

35:56.362 --> 35:59.323
Yeah, go ahead.
Glare at me. Make a bowl for me.

36:00.408 --> 36:03.077
I know all I have to do
is chew and swallow,

36:04.370 --> 36:05.955
but eating is such a hassle.

36:07.290 --> 36:10.084
By the way, your kimchi went bad
and wilted. I threw it out.

36:10.168 --> 36:13.004
I just winged this batch,
but goddamn, it's amazing.

36:14.505 --> 36:16.048
No one's gonna eat this food.

36:16.924 --> 36:18.634
So you just made it to throw it out?

36:18.718 --> 36:20.845
An empty house just doesn't feel right.

36:21.387 --> 36:22.263
I heard

36:23.181 --> 36:25.099
that jerk told his realtor

36:25.183 --> 36:27.351
not to mess with this place
till you move out.

36:28.728 --> 36:31.480
The two of you are driving me up the wall
with this nonsense.

36:32.648 --> 36:33.900
Have some stew, okay?

36:33.983 --> 36:37.069
- But you didn't.
- I'll get a bite at the office.

36:39.113 --> 36:41.324
It's your loss.
This kimchi is pretty good.

36:58.049 --> 37:00.468
Ugh! Damn it! "Just nowww"? "Nowww"?

37:01.219 --> 37:02.762
That's red pepper powder.

37:04.055 --> 37:07.433
Now we're gonna
make these flowers bloom. Follow along.

37:09.894 --> 37:12.146
Like so. You see? Have fun. Be creative.

37:13.022 --> 37:14.065
All right.

37:14.148 --> 37:16.275
Now we'll hold the bottom portion

37:17.401 --> 37:20.863
of the finished flower
with the flower scissors like this

37:21.405 --> 37:23.699
and then slowly remove it from the nail.

37:23.783 --> 37:26.369
Then you find the perfect spot, and…

37:29.163 --> 37:30.373
and there you have it.

37:32.124 --> 37:33.167
Give it a whirl.

37:34.252 --> 37:36.754
God, he's such a master.
That eye for detail.

37:38.589 --> 37:40.216
- Wow, he's so good!
- Oh goodness!

37:40.299 --> 37:42.260
It's so pretty.

37:42.343 --> 37:43.761
It's just a bunch of tricks.

37:43.844 --> 37:46.264
He's not really employing
traditional techniques.

37:47.014 --> 37:49.433
Well, traditions change
over time, don't they?

37:49.517 --> 37:52.103
Oh, by the way,
do you have your new lights?

37:52.895 --> 37:54.647
I would love to come check them out.

37:56.399 --> 37:59.151
'Cause, you know, those are gonna be
one-of-a-kind in South Korea.

37:59.235 --> 38:01.320
I doubt I'd be able to see them otherwise.

38:02.989 --> 38:05.950
Um, I don't know.
I don't really get to decide that.

38:07.410 --> 38:09.078
Well, I will take that as a yes.

38:16.043 --> 38:17.920
- He's great.
- That was great.

38:18.004 --> 38:20.214
I'll be looking forward to the next class.

38:20.298 --> 38:22.008
- Have a good day.
- Bye.

38:22.842 --> 38:26.470
Hey, I DMed you to put in an order.
Rice cakes for Oh Hyeon-cheol.

38:26.554 --> 38:27.430
Oh.

38:27.930 --> 38:29.098
His entire family is…

38:29.181 --> 38:32.435
They're really particular,
so it needs to be perfect, or I'll be…

38:32.518 --> 38:34.562
I'll be on the chopping block
if it goes wrong.

38:35.771 --> 38:36.856
This is your husband?

38:37.815 --> 38:38.858
Huh?

38:38.941 --> 38:40.526
It's an older man's name.

38:41.527 --> 38:43.571
Oh, they're for
my father-in-law's birthday.

38:44.238 --> 38:46.449
Not too excited
to deal with your in-laws, huh?

38:48.409 --> 38:49.577
Don't you worry.

38:49.660 --> 38:51.412
I'll make sure they say,

38:51.495 --> 38:53.998
"Well, this is going all wrong,

38:55.374 --> 38:56.667
but she nailed the rice cakes."

39:02.340 --> 39:03.341
Oh wow.

39:17.897 --> 39:21.734
How'd I get a case
about a 50-million-won piece of luggage?

39:22.234 --> 39:25.696
I got a feeling we're gonna be banging
our heads against the wall with this one.

39:28.240 --> 39:29.325
Fingerprints?

39:29.992 --> 39:32.286
It was underwater,
so it's gonna take a while to know.

39:37.249 --> 39:38.626
Man, what happened?

39:40.419 --> 39:42.171
There's a lot going on out here,

39:42.922 --> 39:44.256
but it's sort of dead too.

39:44.840 --> 39:47.301
It's too clean, like it's been scoured.

39:48.969 --> 39:50.054
What do you mean?

39:52.390 --> 39:53.933
I dunno, man.

39:59.605 --> 40:00.606
Hello?

40:02.316 --> 40:03.692
They know who owned the trunk.

40:09.949 --> 40:12.451
You must have
a whole bunch of these at home

40:12.535 --> 40:15.621
since you didn't notice
this 50-million-won trunk was gone.

40:18.624 --> 40:20.418
Although we know you didn't use it.

40:22.920 --> 40:25.631
When we found the body,
we found this thing with it.

40:31.887 --> 40:35.641
So how are you related
to the owner of the trunk to my left?

40:38.144 --> 40:39.186
I'm her husband.

40:41.480 --> 40:43.023
And my wife used to use it.

40:46.485 --> 40:47.736
Okay, which wife?

40:56.954 --> 40:59.832
You don't have to be here
since I'm around. It's about to get dusty.

41:19.685 --> 41:22.229
Word is,
he's looking for a house in Budapest.

41:25.983 --> 41:27.902
I think he's planning to settle down.

41:38.287 --> 41:40.539
So I'd like to take
the chandelier with me today.

41:41.040 --> 41:42.625
- If that's okay with--
- Sure, go ahead.

41:43.584 --> 41:45.085
You know it's really rare, right?

41:45.169 --> 41:47.505
So you might wanna
talk this over with Jeong-won…

41:49.256 --> 41:51.800
Your husband.
Sorry, I forgot that's who he is to you.

41:51.884 --> 41:54.887
Well, you must know about
the nightmares that thing caused.

41:55.471 --> 41:58.349
Clearly, we needed to get rid of it.
We both agreed on it.

42:00.351 --> 42:02.353
We should have dinner together
with our spouses soon.

42:03.562 --> 42:07.107
Now that the lights are taken care of
and the two of you are officially married,

42:07.191 --> 42:08.359
we should celebrate.

42:09.109 --> 42:10.986
You… We don't have to if it's awkward.

42:11.820 --> 42:14.073
We'd be delighted. I'm glad you asked.

42:14.156 --> 42:15.908
How about next Wednesday, then?

42:16.867 --> 42:18.702
Yeah. That sounds good.

42:21.372 --> 42:22.248
Oh hey!

42:23.624 --> 42:25.209
This is where you're hiding!

42:28.712 --> 42:30.923
My husband has told me so much about you.

42:31.006 --> 42:32.967
Sorry. Kang Yoon-a.

42:33.968 --> 42:34.802
Hi.

42:43.686 --> 42:48.107
She seems really classy.
Super easygoing. She's not a loudmouth.

42:48.649 --> 42:51.318
That's a relief. I mean,
I was worried she was gonna be a lunatic.

42:52.027 --> 42:55.239
I guess Jeong-won's got pretty good taste
in women, after all, doesn't he?

42:57.366 --> 42:58.701
Hey, are you doing okay?

42:59.285 --> 43:00.327
So good.

43:00.869 --> 43:02.705
Jeong-won deserves to be happy too.

43:13.382 --> 43:16.135
We're going to have
Seo-yeon and her husband over for dinner.

43:21.181 --> 43:22.266
Are you guys friends?

43:22.766 --> 43:24.977
Well, she helped out with the chandelier.

43:25.603 --> 43:26.812
So I agreed to it.

44:11.815 --> 44:14.860
I was just going to sell it
to the scrapyard for 3,000 won.

44:16.111 --> 44:18.280
Then she offered to take it off our hands.

44:18.822 --> 44:21.408
3,000? That thing's worth 30 million.

44:22.076 --> 44:24.620
I didn't want us to remember it
as something valuable.

44:25.120 --> 44:27.998
So I thought we should treat it
like a worthless piece of junk

44:28.082 --> 44:30.084
and watch it get melted down
little by little

44:30.167 --> 44:31.543
until there's nothing left.

44:33.295 --> 44:36.131
Now I bet it's gonna be around
for a while. It's frustrating.

44:43.180 --> 44:45.516
Seriously, before you started this,
what did you do?

44:47.559 --> 44:48.686
A lot of things.

44:50.479 --> 44:51.855
Okay, tell me about one.

44:53.691 --> 44:55.651
I taught dance lessons for a while.

44:55.734 --> 44:58.821
Tango, waltz, all that jazz.

44:59.947 --> 45:01.281
Did you teach milonga?

45:04.702 --> 45:06.787
There was a recording I heard in the car.

45:09.915 --> 45:11.333
Where do you go in the morning?

45:14.336 --> 45:15.587
I exercise.

45:16.547 --> 45:17.589
What do you do?

45:21.635 --> 45:22.761
Kayaking.

45:24.304 --> 45:26.306
When I'm out there alone in the morning,

45:26.932 --> 45:29.143
I feel like an island floating on a lake.

45:31.729 --> 45:32.855
You're pretty active.

45:36.442 --> 45:38.736
I tried to improve
our sleeping arrangement.

45:39.486 --> 45:41.864
Think of this as a peaceful little island.

45:43.031 --> 45:45.117
I'll try to keep you safe from the waves.

46:45.427 --> 46:46.637
What are you doing here?

46:48.889 --> 46:50.974
I wanna see the bedroom of our newlyweds.

46:51.558 --> 46:53.227
What are you hoping to see?

46:55.729 --> 46:58.440
It smells so different now.
I think it's that diffuser.

46:58.941 --> 47:00.025
Is it bergamot?

47:00.526 --> 47:02.152
We really like the new lights.

47:02.694 --> 47:03.779
Thank you.

47:04.738 --> 47:06.490
Great. Did you give them a good look?

47:36.311 --> 47:38.564
- Aren't you uncomfortable here?
- What do you mean?

47:39.606 --> 47:41.316
A divorced couple's dinner party?

47:43.235 --> 47:44.194
I guess so.

47:48.866 --> 47:50.325
Dinner is just about ready.

48:35.370 --> 48:37.581
Go ahead. You love these.

48:51.553 --> 48:52.387
When I lived here,

48:52.471 --> 48:55.057
I would've never been able
to serve something like this.

48:55.557 --> 48:57.809
Now that I'm a guest,
I finally get to try it.

48:58.936 --> 49:01.188
I'm sorry. It's so funny.

49:01.271 --> 49:02.481
Please go ahead.

49:02.981 --> 49:04.900
When I heard you liked it,
I made it right away.

49:08.403 --> 49:10.530
Do you hate tomatoes too, then?

49:11.156 --> 49:12.199
How about that?

49:20.165 --> 49:22.542
I figured you'd like them, actually.

49:22.626 --> 49:24.503
I mean, most people do.

49:34.012 --> 49:35.681
You've got something here, honey.

49:51.947 --> 49:54.157
So, Jeong-won, when did you meet Seo-yeon?

49:57.285 --> 49:58.912
It was about 30 years ago.

49:58.996 --> 50:00.789
Mm-hmm. That's right.

50:01.289 --> 50:02.332
Wow.

50:02.958 --> 50:05.794
And yet you were only actually married
about two years.

50:06.962 --> 50:10.048
Guess even 30 years of build-up
can't save a marriage

50:10.132 --> 50:11.341
if it's not a good fit.

50:16.346 --> 50:19.725
Guess it goes to show you really just need
to find the right person.

50:23.979 --> 50:26.106
- You need to--
- What, I can't say that?

50:26.606 --> 50:28.692
Are you just gonna sit here and pretend?

50:37.284 --> 50:40.203
How about you? Before you got married,
how long did you date?

50:41.329 --> 50:42.164
So…

50:44.166 --> 50:46.001
that didn't really affect us since we…

50:49.838 --> 50:51.882
had so much chemistry right away.

50:53.633 --> 50:55.260
Wasn't it the same for you guys?

51:23.080 --> 51:23.997
I'm handsome

51:25.957 --> 51:26.917
and young.

51:28.710 --> 51:30.587
Nice and tall too.

51:32.798 --> 51:33.882
What are you doing?

51:36.093 --> 51:37.594
As in what am I doing for work?

51:37.677 --> 51:39.137
You wanna know what I "do"?

51:39.221 --> 51:41.056
You could interpret it that way.

51:42.724 --> 51:44.101
You're wound tight.

51:46.436 --> 51:47.896
Are you in love with In-ji?

51:52.484 --> 51:54.194
Why can't you answer the question?

51:57.030 --> 51:58.198
Just so you know,

51:59.741 --> 52:00.909
I love Seo-yeon.

52:08.375 --> 52:09.751
We've had quite a bit of wine.

52:13.338 --> 52:14.464
How's it work for you guys?

52:15.382 --> 52:19.052
Usually, we like to do it
after we've had… three glasses or so.

52:22.013 --> 52:23.473
Are you two like us?

52:32.190 --> 52:34.359
We're a beer couple, actually.

52:38.238 --> 52:40.532
Oh! Beer. Cool.

52:42.659 --> 52:45.787
Well, they've got us there.
Different alcohol content.

52:53.336 --> 52:56.131
I prefer the one you had in here before.
Don't you?

53:03.513 --> 53:04.764
Uh, no.

53:06.892 --> 53:09.019
This is why
I thought you were childish.

53:10.061 --> 53:11.313
Holding onto the past,

53:11.813 --> 53:14.608
licking old wounds,
and losing sleep over old stories.

53:16.193 --> 53:17.110
Don't you agree?

53:18.486 --> 53:21.573
I should've hauled that piece of garbage
over to the fucking junkyard.

53:27.662 --> 53:30.123
Truth is, there are some things
you don't just get over.

53:30.207 --> 53:31.416
Don't minimize his pain.

53:37.839 --> 53:38.965
Jeez, so serious.

53:39.049 --> 53:42.052
There have gotta be some old wounds
you're still nursing. Am I wrong?

53:44.679 --> 53:45.764
Nothing?

53:57.067 --> 53:58.026
Let's call it.

53:59.027 --> 54:02.197
I don't want this dinner party…
to peter out.

54:57.460 --> 55:00.130
Have you seen
the USB drive I keep in the car?

55:00.213 --> 55:01.172
I can't find it.

55:08.305 --> 55:10.015
Bluetooth's not your thing, huh?

55:10.098 --> 55:12.767
I guess I don't leave a trace or a name.

55:16.396 --> 55:18.106
You don't use Bluetooth either.

55:20.567 --> 55:22.527
I've always used USB to store my work.

55:23.111 --> 55:25.655
No security issues,
and Bluetooth's a hassle.

55:27.574 --> 55:28.950
I'll reconnect your drive.

55:30.368 --> 55:31.870
That song just never gets old.

55:34.039 --> 55:36.166
And you actually dance to that song?

55:38.460 --> 55:39.294
Tango?

55:43.298 --> 55:45.592
Sorry. It's just hard to understand how…

55:45.675 --> 55:47.302
I thought you'd hate that stuff.

55:47.886 --> 55:49.929
I mean, it's hard to picture you dancing.
That's all.

55:55.852 --> 55:58.730
Oh, I'm sorry. That sounded harsh.

56:01.649 --> 56:05.195
I bet it would blow you away.
If only I could show you.

56:37.227 --> 56:39.229
Okay, would you mind showing me?

57:06.005 --> 57:07.006
What's this?

57:07.590 --> 57:09.426
It takes two to tango, obviously.

57:09.509 --> 57:10.969
Uh, no, no, no, no.

57:11.511 --> 57:12.554
Uh…

57:14.305 --> 57:16.433
Your right hand rests on the woman's back,

57:17.725 --> 57:20.937
and your left hand should always
support the woman's right hand.

57:21.521 --> 57:23.106
Uh, do we really have to…

57:23.189 --> 57:26.609
Now we shift our center of gravity
one step after another.

57:30.905 --> 57:33.658
As you take each step,
try not to go by yourself.

57:33.741 --> 57:35.618
Imagine carrying the other person with you

57:35.702 --> 57:38.204
so our bodies can transition
through the space.

57:42.667 --> 57:45.211
Now move forward on your right foot
two steps. That's it.

57:45.295 --> 57:46.546
Right foot. Oh!

57:49.632 --> 57:51.009
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

57:51.968 --> 57:54.971
Starting with your right foot,
take a step forward.

57:55.930 --> 57:56.806
Left foot.

57:58.016 --> 57:59.100
Right foot sidesteps.

58:01.352 --> 58:04.063
We're shifting our center. And step right.

58:05.523 --> 58:06.900
- Oh!
- Oh!

58:09.777 --> 58:10.820
Try again.
